    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-74574: cot²θ=(cscθ−1)(cscθ+1), so cancellation gives cosθ on the original expression's domain. q-78951: dy/dx=2cot t; differentiating with respect to t and dividing by dx/dt=sin t gives −2csc³t. q-123003: (48t³)/(2t)=24t², which is 24 at t=1. q-120532: csc x=−2 gives degree solutions 210 and 330, whose product is 69300. q-29004: sin x=√3/2 gives π/3 and 2π/3, whose product is 2π²/9. q-120556: with α=arcsin(1/6), the solutions are π+α and 2π−α; their product rounds to 20.2. q-29938: with α=arcsin(4/5) in degrees, the solutions are α and 180−α; their product rounds to 6741. The source's intermediate rounding does not change either requested rounded answer. q-29477: only 1/3 lies outside the cosecant range. q-66005: the equations reduce to cosecant values −1/3, 10, and 6, so only I has no solution. q-29207: cot x=1 gives π/4 and 5π/4, with product 5π²/16. q-69945: the area is |(−1)(6)−(3)(−2)|=0. q-42381: dimensions 3×2, 2×3, and 1×3 permit only OP. q-22055: dimensions 2×2, 2×3, and 3×3 permit XY and YZ but not YX. q-129480: (5×7)(7×1) produces 5×1. q-77476: (3×1)(1×3) produces 3×3. q-77475: (1×3)(3×1) produces 1×1. Each MA finding is supported by worked-solution evidence; no captured grading evidence is supplied.",
